>Seriously, what do people think of a dwarf class?
     I'd expand this out, actually... it doesn't make much sense to me to
have "elf" as a separate class, since it's a question of race/species/kind of
critter, as opposed to occupation, like Archaelogist/Tourist/Knight/Valkyrie
etc. Sometimes I'd like to play an elven healer, sometimes I'd like to play
an elven warrior, but I'd generally like to always play an elf. You get lots
of intrinsics thattaway. :)
     So maybe you could swipe the idea from Moria to have "species" as
a settable character option. Have human, elf, dwarf, gnome, hobbit, orc,
troll... are there any other sentient species in the dungeon that would be
good for player characters?

